==Round of 16==

===France vs Argentina===
[[File:FRA-ARG (21).jpg|thumb|Match referee [[Alireza Faghani]] presents one of eight [[Penalty card|yellow cards]] during the match.]]
The teams had faced each other in 11 previous matches, including two World Cup group stage matches, both won by Argentina ([[1930 FIFA World Cup Group 1#Argentina vs France|1–0]] in 1930, and [[1978 FIFA World Cup Group 1#Argentina vs France|2–1]] in 1978).<ref name="statistical kit">{{cite web |url=https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/34cfdea0e0f99b9c/original/yordczhbifo8h92guz7u-pdf.pdf |title=Statistical Kit for the FIFA World Cup |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |access-date=2 July 2018}}</ref>

After nine minutes, [[Antoine Griezmann]]'s 25-yard free-kick crashed back off [[Franco Armani]]'s crossbar. After picking the ball up deep inside his own half, [[Kylian Mbappé]] set off on a run that was halted when [[Marcos Rojo]] hauled him down just inside the area. Griezmann stepped up and converted from the spot, sending the ball low to Armani's right. Four minutes before the interval, [[Ángel Di María]] shot from distance with his left foot to beat [[Hugo Lloris]] into the top right corner of the net. Three minutes after the restart, [[Éver Banega]]'s free-kick was headed out towards [[Lionel Messi]] whose effort towards goal from the right was diverted past Lloris by [[Gabriel Mercado]] with his left leg. Nine minutes later, [[Lucas Hernandez]]'s cross from the left found [[Benjamin Pavard]], who shot a half-volley from outside the area, sending it into Armani's top-right corner. Pavard’s goal was later voted the best [[FIFA World Cup awards#Goal of the Tournament|goal of the tournament]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2018-07-25 |title=2018 FIFA World Cup Russia™ - News - Pavard's stunner voted Hyundai Goal of the Tournament - FIFA.com |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/pavard-s-stunner-voted-hyundai-goal-of-the-tournament |access-date=2025-04-25 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180725163638/https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/pavard-s-stunner-voted-hyundai-goal-of-the-tournament |archive-date=25 July 2018 }}</ref> Mbappé put France ahead again in the 64th minute when he picked up a loose ball in the left of the area, found a yard of space and fired in low with his left foot under Armani. His second – a first-time low finish from the right of the penalty area with his right foot – followed just four minutes later.<ref name="Goal France v Argentina">{{cite web |last1=Atkinson |first1=Guy |title=Mbappe turns on the style to dump out Messi's men |url=http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/france-v-argentina/66pdxwjvvzjy3f5r6fqcy7d9l |publisher=Goal.com |date=30 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180710090326/http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/france-v-argentina/66pdxwjvvzjy3f5r6fqcy7d9l |archive-date=10 July 2018}}</ref> [[Sergio Agüero]] nodded home in the third minute of stoppage time from a Messi cross from the right.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Jennings |first1=Patrick |title=BBC France 4 Argentina 3 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44439354 |publisher=BBC Sport |date=30 June 2018 }}</ref> Argentina, however, was unable to equalize to send the match to extra-time from being eliminated of the tournament .<ref>{{cite web |last1=Steinberg |first1=Jacob |title=Guardian France 4 Argentina 3 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2018/jun/30/world-cup-2018-france-v-argentina-live?page=with:block-5b37a6c1e4b0c089ab2b8052#block-5b37a6c1e4b0c089ab2b8052 |work=The Guardian |date=30 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180710090326/https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2018/jun/30/world-cup-2018-france-v-argentina-live?page=with:block-5b37a6c1e4b0c089ab2b8052#block-5b37a6c1e4b0c089ab2b8052 |archive-date=10 July 2018}}</ref> This game was hailed as "one of the greatest World Cup games of all time" by ''[[The Independent]]''.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Liew |first1=Jonathan |title=Why France vs Argentina was one of the greatest World Cup games of all time |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/world-cup-2018-france-vs-argentina-great-games-of-all-time-kylian-mbappe-lionel-messi-a8425386.html |work=The Independent |date=30 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180710090326/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/world-cup-2018-france-vs-argentina-great-games-of-all-time-kylian-mbappe-lionel-messi-a8425386.html |archive-date=10 July 2018}}</ref>

With this match, [[Didier Deschamps]] became the longest-serving coach in the history of the France national team with his 80th game in charge of France, moving ahead of his predecessor [[Raymond Domenech]].<ref name="FRA-ARG recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/review-france--argentina-2978977 |title=France into quarter-finals after seven-goal thriller |publisher=FIFA |date=30 June 2018 |access-date=30 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520053317/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/review-france--argentina-2978977 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> Mbappé became the first teenager to score at least twice in a World Cup tournament since [[Michael Owen]] in 1998, and the first teenager to score at least twice in a single World Cup match since [[Pelé]] netted twice for Brazil against Sweden in the [[1958 FIFA World Cup final|1958 final]]. Argentina became the first team to score at least three goals but still lose a World Cup match since the [[1986 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Soviet Union vs Belgium|Soviet Union vs Belgium]] in 1986, and was also the first time that Argentina had been eliminated in the round of 16 since [[1994 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Romania vs Argentina|1994]], when they were defeated by [[Romania national football team|Romania]].<ref name="Goal France v Argentina"/>

