===Uruguay vs Portugal===
[[File:URU-POR (17).jpg|thumb|The Uruguayan team celebrates after [[Edinson Cavani]] scores his team's second goal in the 62nd minute.]]
The teams had met in two previous matches, most recently in [[Brazil Independence Cup]] in 1972, the match ending in a 1–1 draw.<ref name="statistical kit"/>

In the seventh minute, [[Edinson Cavani]] switched play from right to left with a sweeping pass out to [[Luis Suárez]], who delivered a cross which the former crashed home at the back post from six yards out. In the 55th minute, [[Raphaël Guerreiro]] delivered a cross from a short corner on the left, which [[Pepe (footballer, born 1983)|Pepe]] finished with a downward header. Just seven minutes later, [[Rodrigo Bentancur]] collected the ball around 30 yards out and slipped a pass out to Cavani on the left side of the penalty area, Cavani then shot a [[Curl (football)|curling]] right-foot strike into the right corner of the net to reclaim the lead for Uruguay. [[Bernardo Silva]] shot off-target with the goal gaping after [[Fernando Muslera]]'s mistake, with Cavani seeming to pick up an injury in the scramble.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Smith |first1=Jamie |title=Cavani brace sends tearful Ronaldo home early |url=http://www.goal.com/en/match/uruguay-v-portugal/66lsube18siy28cytac5ja8kp |publisher=Goal.com |date=30 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180701164901/http://www.goal.com/en/match/uruguay-v-portugal/66lsube18siy28cytac5ja8kp |archive-date=1 July 2018}}</ref>

Pepe, aged 35 years and 124 days, became Portugal's oldest goal-scorer at a FIFA World Cup.<ref name="URU-POR recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/cavani-fires-la-celeste-past-european-champions-2979265 |title=Cavani fires La Celeste past European champions |publisher=FIFA |date=30 June 2018 |access-date=30 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520053354/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/cavani-fires-la-celeste-past-european-champions-2979265 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> This was the first time Uruguay won their opening four games at a World Cup tournament since 1930, with the fourth game in that run being their [[1930 FIFA World Cup Final|4–2]] victory over Argentina in the final.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Rose |first1=Gary |title=Uruguay 2 Portugal 1 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44439361 |publisher=BBC Sport |date=30 June 2018 }}</ref>

