===Colombia vs England===
[[File:FWC 2018 - Round of 16 - COL v ENG - Photo 132.jpg|thumb|right|[[Eric Dier]] scores the winning goal in England's first [[List of FIFA World Cup penalty shoot-outs|World Cup penalty shoot-out]] victory, having lost thrice before.]]
The teams had faced each other in five previous matches, including one World Cup group stage match in 1998, a [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group G#Colombia vs England|2–0]] England win. Their most recent meeting came in a friendly in 2005, a 3–2 England win.<ref name="statistical kit"/>

In the 16th minute, [[Harry Kane]] arrived beyond the back post to meet a [[Kieran Trippier]] cross, but was unable to direct his header on target. [[Wilmar Barrios]] was booked when he appeared to headbutt [[Jordan Henderson]] in the build-up to a free-kick Trippier bent narrowly wide. Colombia gave away a penalty early in the second half when [[Carlos Sánchez (Colombian footballer)|Carlos Sánchez]] dragged Kane down in the box after a corner from the right. Kane scored from 12 yards, shooting down the middle to give England the lead. Colombia forced their way into extra time, [[Yerry Mina]] scoring a downward header from a [[Juan Cuadrado]] corner from the right in injury time. [[Eric Dier]] scored the final penalty in the shoot-out, with England coming back from 3–2 down after [[Mateus Uribe]] and [[Carlos Bacca]] failed to convert their spot-kicks.<ref name="COL-ENG recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/england-into-quarter-finals-after-penalty-shootout-2981878 |title=England into quarter-finals after penalty shootout |publisher=FIFA |date=3 July 2018 |access-date=3 July 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520063003/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/england-into-quarter-finals-after-penalty-shootout-2981878 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Smith |first1=Jamie |title=Dier seals shoot-out glory for Three Lions |url=http://www.goal.com/en/match/colombia-v-england/68fhe8lgzak2gx5tn74k8kusp |publisher=Goal.com |date=3 July 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180704024209/http://www.goal.com/en/match/colombia-v-england/68fhe8lgzak2gx5tn74k8kusp |archive-date=4 July 2018}}</ref>

This was the first time that England had won a [[List of FIFA World Cup penalty shoot-outs|penalty shoot-out]] at the FIFA World Cup, and only the second time they had won on penalties at any major tournament (the previous occasion being [[UEFA Euro 1996 knockout stage#Spain vs England|against Spain at Euro 1996]]). Kane became the first player to score in six consecutive England appearances since [[Tommy Lawton]] did so in 1939. England conceded in injury time at the end of the second half for the first time in World Cup history, with Mina's goal coming after 92 minutes and 33 seconds.<ref>{{cite web |last1=McNulty |first1=Phil |title=England beat Colombia 4–3 on penalties |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44610244 |website=BBC Sport |publisher=BBC |access-date=3 July 2018 |date=3 July 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180703210750/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44610244 |archive-date=3 July 2018}}</ref>

