==Match for third place==
[[File:Belgium_2-0_England,_BEL_line-up.jpg|thumb|Belgium line-up before the start of the game]]
[[Belgium national football team|Belgium]] and [[England national football team|England]] had previously met in 22 matches, including three matches at the World Cup, one round of 16 game at the [[1990 FIFA World Cup]] which ended in a [[1990 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#England vs Belgium|1–0]] victory for England, one group stage game at the [[1954 FIFA World Cup]] which ended in a [[1954 FIFA World Cup Group 4#England vs Belgium|4–4]] draw and their most recent encounter in Group G of this tournament which Belgium won [[2018 FIFA World Cup Group G#England vs Belgium|1–0]].<ref name="statistical kit"/> As both were European teams, this was already set pre-match as the [[European nations at the FIFA World Cup#Overview|10th consecutive World Cup in which European teams finished third]], stretching back to [[1982 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Match for third place|1982]].

After four minutes, [[Thomas Meunier]] raced into the box to get across [[Danny Rose (footballer, born 1990)|Danny Rose]] and tucked home [[Nacer Chadli]]'s low cross in from the left from six yards out. [[Harry Kane]] scuffed wide of the left post, from a [[Raheem Sterling]] lay-off. In the 70th minute, [[Eric Dier]] burst through for a one-on-one and dinked over [[Thibaut Courtois]], only to see a retreating [[Toby Alderweireld]] hack the ball off the line. [[Jordan Pickford]] made a one-handed save to deny Meunier in the 80th minute. [[Eden Hazard]] scored the second with a near-post finish with his right foot, having been sent clean through by [[Kevin De Bruyne]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Dorman |first1=Matt |title=Meunier, Hazard make history for Martinez's entertainers |url=http://www.goal.com/en/match/belgium-v-england/3dm9d0sw90igwqwoqs2fbfi7d |publisher=Goal.com |date=14 July 2018}}</ref>

Meunier was the 10th player to score for Belgium at the 2018 World Cup. No other team had more, equalling France in 1982 and Italy in 2006.<ref name="BEL-ENG recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/hazard-meunier-bag-bronze-for-belgium |title=Hazard, Meunier bag bronze for Belgium |publisher=FIFA |date=14 July 2018 |access-date=14 July 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520063745/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/hazard-meunier-bag-bronze-for-belgium |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> This became Belgium's best finish at a World Cup, having previously finished fourth in 1986. This was England's 100th match at a major tournament – 69 at the World Cup and 31 at the European Championship. Since 1966, no player had been involved in more World Cup goals for Belgium than Hazard (seven – three goals and four assists), level with [[Jan Ceulemans]] (also four goals and three assists).<ref>{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |title=World Cup 2018: England finish fourth after Belgium defeat |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44748604 |work=BBC Sport |date=14 July 2018}}</ref>

